# Unit character assets — drop the Blue Archive art/models here.
# Served at /units/<name> (this folder is Vite's public root).
#
# The game tries assets in this order and falls back gracefully:
#   1. <key>.glb  -> animated 3D model   (best — real walk/sprint/dodge/fire)
#   2. <key>.png  -> flat 2D billboard   (still character art, no animation)
#   3. built-in procedural placeholder   (labelled stand-in, always works)
#
# Keys / characters / weapons:
#   saori    -> Unit 1 / Machine Gun  (M4A1)
#   hoshino  -> Unit 2 / Shotgun      (XM1014)
#   aru      -> Unit 3 / Sniper Rifle (PSG1)
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3D MODELS (preferred) — saori.glb / hoshino.glb / aru.glb
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   - Format: glTF binary (.glb), Y-up, real-world-ish upright humanoid rig.
#   - NOT Draco-compressed (no Draco decoder is wired up). Export uncompressed.
#   - Auto-fitted in-engine: scaled to a set height, feet planted, centered —
#     so the model's native scale/origin don't matter.
#   - Animation clips are matched by NAME (case-insensitive substring). Name
#     your clips so they contain one of these keywords:
#         idle   : idle / stand / wait
#         walk   : walk / move
#         sprint : run / sprint
#         dodge  : dodge / roll / evade / avoid / step / dash
#         fire   : fire / shoot / attack / atk / shot / skill
#     Missing clips degrade gracefully (sprint->walk->idle, etc.). A model with
#     no clips still renders, just static.
#   - Facing: the model is turned to face its target automatically. If a model
#     ends up facing the WRONG way (back to the enemy), flip UNIT_MODEL_YAW_OFFSET
#     in client/src/main.js between Math.PI and 0.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2D BILLBOARDS (fallback) — saori.png / hoshino.png / aru.png
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   - PNG, TRANSPARENT background (alpha cutout). Portrait, full body, feet near
#     the BOTTOM edge (sprite is anchored at the feet). ~512x768 / 2:3 ratio.
